cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "mbariml: a curation pipeline for turning deep-sea imagery and video into object-detection training data"
abstract: >-
  A Python pipeline for turning deep-sea imagery and video into object-detection
  training data. It runs an Ultralytics YOLO model over stills or video, stores
  every detection as a reviewable region of interest, groups those regions by
  visual similarity so a human can accept or reject them in bulk, and exports the
  result as training data, statistics, identification sidecars, and galleries.
type: software
